{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): Good afternoon, doctor. Please excuse me, I am a little late. The rain near Gandhi market was very heavy and the auto was simply not moving.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Afternoon. Uh, sit. One minute, this computer is hanging again.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (PATIENT): Certainly, doctor. There is no hurry. My grandson kept me at home also. He played cricket yesterday, under-fourteen, and he took two wickets, so he has been talking since morning.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Two wickets. Mm. Who were they playing?",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (PATIENT): The corporation school side, doctor. Now he is asking for a new bat. I told him after the exams only.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ha, fair. Right. Sorry, I only half heard you at the door. What brings you today? Say it again.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (PATIENT): Doctor, I have come for my review. I am worried about my kidneys.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Kidneys, yes. You are the diabetic with the kidney problem. Nurse, err, read the creatinine and the eGFR. I am on the wrong screen.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (NURSE): Serum creatinine is 1.8 milligrams per decilitre. eGFR is 41.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): 41. Say the eGFR once more, the fan is loud.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (NURSE): eGFR 41, doctor. Creatinine 1.8.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (PATIENT): I understand. Last year at the camp they told me the kidney test was borderline only. I have been thinking of that.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Borderline at the camp, yes. Umm, are you still taking the ramipril?",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes doctor. Remipril, five milligrams, one tablet every morning, for the pressure and for the kidneys. That tablet I never miss.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ramipril, five milligrams, every morning. Continue that. And the sugar medicine? I have lost the line here.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (PATIENT): Metformin, doctor. Five hundred milligrams in the morning and at night.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (NURSE): Doctor, his daughter was at the desk. She said he does not take the tablets on Sundays.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): No, sister, with respect, that is not correct, it is Saturday, not Sunday. On Saturday morning I go to the temple, so I miss only the morning sugar tablet. The ramipril I take on Saturday also. I am sorry for the mix-up.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Saturday, morning metformin, temple. Ramipril still taken. Uh, did you get the pressure checked?",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes doctor. Sister told me just now, it is 152 over 88.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (NURSE): That is right. Blood pressure 152 over 88, pulse 74. I took both just now.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. Any wound that is slow to heal? With the sugar we have to ask.",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (NURSE): There was a small cut on the left shin. It healed in five days.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes doctor. That little cut closed in five days, quite in the normal way. There is no slow healing.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): So that is not a slow wound. The knee, tell me again, I was typing. What is the pain and what are you taking?",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (PATIENT): The right knee has been paining for some months, doctor. I cannot say exactly when it began. I have been buying brufin from the medical shop, 400 milligrams, two times a day when it pains. You had advised me not to take it. I apologise.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): I had a look, the right knee is a little bony, no heat and no swelling. I think it is ordinary wear and tear. Stop the ibuprofen, with an eGFR of 41 it is not safe, and I am prescribing paracetamol, one gram by mouth, up to three times a day, only when the knee pains. Continue the ramipril five milligrams every morning, and do not buy ibuprofen from the shop again.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (PATIENT): Yes doctor. I will stop the brufin from today itself, and I will take only the paracetamol. Kindly say when I should return.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): Before that, chest or breathing, any trouble?",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (PATIENT): No doctor. The chest and the breathing are quite alright.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): Good. Reception will book the review in three months, and we will repeat the creatinine and the eGFR before you come."
 ],
